1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,192
How does a seller with no website take a card payment?

2
00:00:03,242 --> 00:00:07,440
Some sellers take orders in a messenger, and have no website code at all.

3
00:00:07,490 --> 00:00:11,280
For them, a payment link is like a bill with a pay here button.

4
00:00:11,330 --> 00:00:19,536
A merchant admin or operator makes one in the portal, for one of its live websites: an amount, what it is for, and how long it works.

5
00:00:19,586 --> 00:00:24,096
Behind it is an ordinary payment, and the website's limits still apply.

6
00:00:24,146 --> 00:00:28,080
The link is shown once, and the bank keeps only its fingerprint.

7
00:00:28,130 --> 00:00:31,752
The buyer pays on the same bank page as any other payment.

8
00:00:31,802 --> 00:00:34,560
And a link nobody pays in time is closed.

9
00:00:34,610 --> 00:00:36,480
Next: giving money back.
